 ## Background
-Hierarchical 3D Sampling was introduced in the context of real-time previewing for volume visualization [S1]. The method builds on 2D ordered dithering techniques used in digital halftoning [S1]. The irregular variant, Hierarchical Poisson-disk sampling, was proposed by McCool and Fiume [S1]. The technique is used for density control in volume rendering, serving as an alternative to opacity control or for managing the total number of rendered primitives (LOD) [S1].
